OL,3,GLondon & South East
OL,4,
OL,5,CToday:FSunny spells and dry to start.
OL,6,FCloud increasing through the day, with
OL,7,Fa chance of the odd isolated light
OL,8,Fshower in the afternoon, though most
OL,9,Fwill remain dry. Breezy to start,
OL,10,Fespecially near coasts, then winds
OL,11,Ffalling light.
OL,12,
OL,13,CTonight:FDry with some clear spells
OL,14,Fthrough the evening and overnight.
OL,15,FLight winds throughout. Feeling rather
OL,16,Fchilly, especially in rural spots.
OL,17,
OL,18,CThursday:FA dry and bright but mostly
OL,19,Fcloudy day. Cloud will thicken into
OL,20,Fthe evening as outbreaks of rain
OL,21,Fspread eastward on a freshening breeze.
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
